docs(workflow): bake ui-walkthrough driver into verify agents

Make `just ui-walkthrough` (navigate + per-step screenshot AND accessibility
dump inspection) the default verification for view-touching stories/features,
replacing the single static screenshot, and direct verifiers to actively hunt
concrete bug classes.

- verify-story.md: trigger the driver walkthrough by changed `Hanahuac/Views/**`
  files (not solely an opt-in `## Visual Verification` section); author a focused
  per-story action script, run the driver, inspect every NNN-step.png + .json;
  keep launch+single-screenshot / unit-tested-logic as the sim-unavailable
  fallback.
- verify-feature.md: replace the single end-to-end screenshot with a broad
  multi-screen walkthrough navigating each affected flow; keep the existing
  fallback (the prior "No tap automation" note) as the fallback path.
- Both agents: enumerate bug classes to fail + loop back on — empty a11y tree
  (crash/app-gone), untranslated text in a non-English locale, and
  duplicated/missing/obscured/overlapping controls — not merely confirm the UI
  "matches the spec." References `.workflow/ui-walkthrough/README.md` incl. the
  story-001 `pinch` action.

Agent-definition/doc edits only; no app code. lint + test green.

